        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "contentType": "raw",
        "rawContentType": "JSON",
        "body": "={\n  \"model\": \"google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it:free\",\n  \"max_tokens\": 500,\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"You are an intake assistant for a UK recruitment agency. Extract structured data from a raw enquiry (email, chat/LinkedIn-style message, or web form message). Respond with ONLY valid JSON, no prose, no markdown fences, matching exactly this schema:\\n{\\n  \\\"contact_name\\\": string|null,\\n  \\\"contact_email\\\": string|null,\\n  \\\"contact_phone\\\": string|null,\\n  \\\"company\\\": string|null,\\n  \\\"role_sought\\\": string|null,\\n  \\\"location\\\": string|null,\\n  \\\"salary_budget\\\": string|null,\\n  \\\"urgency\\\": \\\"immediate\\\"|\\\"soon\\\"|\\\"unspecified\\\",\\n  \\\"enquiry_type\\\": \\\"job_requisition\\\"|\\\"general_question\\\"|\\\"admin_request\\\"|\\\"unclear\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": string,\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": number\\n}\\nRules:\\n- enquiry_type is \\\"job_requisition\\\" ONLY if they are asking to hire/recruit for a role.\\n- If the message is an administrative request (e.g. asking to resend a document, asking about an invoice), use \\\"admin_request\\\" and leave role/location/salary as null.\\n- If you cannot determine what the sender wants, use \\\"unclear\\\".\\n- contact_email/contact_phone: extract from the message text if the sender provided one; null if not present.\\n- confidence is your own 0-1 estimate of how confident you are in this extraction given the available text.\\n- Use the submitted name/company fields as a fallback for contact_name/company if the message text doesn't mention them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Source: {{ $json.source }}\\nSubmitted name: {{ $json.name }}\\nSubmitted company: {{ $json.company }}\\nMessage:\\n{{ $json.raw_text }}\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n",
        "options": {}
      },
